-- title:
--   Transcendence degree one: F algebraic over K(t) for any transcendental t
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $F$ be fields with $F$ a $K$-algebra, and let $x \in F$ be an element such that $F$ is algebraic over the intermediate field $K(x) =$ `IntermediateField.adjoin K {x}` generated by $x$ over $K$ inside $F$. Let $t \in F$ be transcendental over $K$, i.e. $t$ is not a root of any nonzero polynomial over $K$ (`Transcendental K t`). The conclusion is that $F$ is algebraic over the intermediate field $K(t) =$ `IntermediateField.adjoin K {t}`: every element of $F$ satisfies a nonzero polynomial with coefficients in $K(t)$. No hypothesis of transcendence on $x$ is imposed; the two hypotheses together force $x$ to be transcendental over $K$, since otherwise $F$ would be algebraic over $K$ and no transcendental $t$ could exist. No assumption is made on the characteristic of $K$, and $t$ is not assumed to lie in $K(x)$ or to be related to $x$ in any way.
--
--   This is the statement that in an extension of transcendence degree one every element transcendental over the base generates a subfield over which the whole extension is algebraic; it is the standard device for replacing a fixed coordinate $x$ of a function field of one variable by an arbitrary uniformiser. It is used throughout the treatment of places and differentials of algebraic curves, for instance in the lemmas on orders and differential coefficients at a place.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_isAlgebraic_adjoin_of_transcendental.lean

import Mathlib.FieldTheory.IntermediateField.Adjoin.Defs
import Mathlib.RingTheory.Algebraic.Defs

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

theorem AlgebraicCurve.isAlgebraic_adjoin_of_transcendental {K F : Type*} [Field K] [Field F] [Algebra K F] (x : F)
    [Algebra.IsAlgebraic (IntermediateField.adjoin K ({x} : Set F)) F] {t : F} (ht : Transcendental K t) :
    Algebra.IsAlgebraic (IntermediateField.adjoin K ({t} : Set F)) F := by sorry
